    "https://jobs.charlotte.edu/postings/69741": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "UNC Charlotte Applicant Site | Cybersecurity, Digital Engineering &amp; AI Innovation Lab &amp; Facility Manager Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Application Process State of NC Salary Chart Campus Security Report Student Employment Cybersecurity, Digital Engineering & AI Innovation Lab & Facility Manager Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check and/or a Motor Vehicle Report The Search Committee will not contact references without first verifying permission with the finalist. Please ensure your resume reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers to the supplemental questions. UNC Charlotte Benefits Information: https://hr.charlotte.edu/benefits/benefits-overview/ Position Information General Information Position Number 001967 Vacancy Open to All Candidates Working Title Cybersecurity, Digital Engineering & AI Innovation Lab & Facility Manager Position Designation EHRA Non-Faculty Employment Type Permanent - Full-time Months per Year 12 Work Schedule 8:00 am – 5:00 pm; Monday – Friday with occasional evening and weekend hours required, as necessary. Hours per week 40 FLSA Status Exempt Division Research Department Div of Research (Adm) Work Location Brevard Street Building Salary Range $98,748 - $120,000 Primary Purpose of Department The Office of Research Protections and Integrity ( ORPI ) is part of the Division of Research. It provides oversight, education, and support for integrity and compliance issues related to research and certain University operations at UNC Charlotte. The office ensures compliance with federal, state, and local applicable policies and laws on human subjects research, animal subjects research, biosafety, conflict of interest and commitment, research misconduct, responsible conduct of research, export control, and research security. Primary Purpose of Position The Cybersecurity, Digital Engineering & AI Innovation Lab & Facility Manager provides operational leadership for the lab and facility. This role is the primary technical and administrative lead for the facility and serves as the essential link between the University, Division of Research, and the North Tryon Tech Hub. The position focuses on managing sophisticated research environments, overseeing building operations, and facilitating technical engagement with industry partners and regional initiatives. The manager has direct responsibility for the facility, including the digital infrastructure required for modern engineering workflows, and holds master key access to secure areas. Research Lab Facility & Building Operations – 50% Technical Innovation & Support – 20% Planning and Organizing Work – 10% Administrative & Fiscal Management – 20% Summary of Position Responsibilities Research Lab Facility & Building Operations Operational Oversight: Manage daily activities of all classrooms, labs, and specialized structures, ensuring 24/7 operational readiness for sensitive data, AI workloads, and Digital Engineering simulations. Building Liaison: Act as the lead coordinator and liaison to University Facilities Management for all building/lab infrastructure needs, including high-capacity power, specialized cooling for AI clusters, and high-bandwidth data networking. Space & Access Management: Oversee all lab and office assignments; manage advanced security protocols and building access for faculty and industry collaborators using systems like Archibus. Inventory & Security: Serve as the primary inventory manager for all equipment; maintain records for both physical devices and virtualized assets/software licenses required for Digital Engineering. Outreach: Organize and direct outreach activities, including tours and demonstrations of Digital Twin models and AI-driven research for industry partners and research sponsors. Technical Innovation & Support Digital Engineering Integration: Oversee the deployment and maintenance of Model-Based Systems Engineering ( MBSE ) tools and collaborative digital environments that allow for the virtual design, testing, and validation of complex systems. Expert Troubleshooting: Oversee the maintenance and repair of complex electronic, mechanical, and data systems; provide tier-one support for Digital Engineering software suites and high-performance computing ( HPC ) interfaces. Safety & Compliance: Establish and enforce rigorous safety standards tailored to the unique risks of the lab (e.g., technical systems, high-voltage data centers, and cyber-physical security). Planning and Organizing Work Strategic Planning: Assist leadership in determining long-range plans for core facilities based on strategic assessments of growth opportunities in digital transformation and AI, in alignment with the Division of Research strategic plan. Modernization Planning: Develop 3-year rolling plans for equipment staging, facility retrofitting, and digital toolchain upgrades to keep the Innovation Lab at the forefront of the Tech Hub’s requirements. Evaluate performance and cost options for system upgrades to maintain a “State-of-the-Art” status in virtual engineering environments. Safety & Security: Serve as the building liaison and safety officer, coordinating security protocols for both physical assets and intellectual property stored within the digital lab environment. Administrative & Fiscal Management Budgetary Authority: Manage the overall lab operations budget and develop justifications for major capital equipment purchases and enterprise-level software subscriptions. Procurement & Vendor Relations: Serve as the primary contact for vendors; evaluate quotes for new equipment, cloud service providers, service contracts, delivery schedules, and specialized installations. Minimum Education/Experience Bachelor’s degree from an appropriately accredited institution, preferably in computer science, systems engineering, information technology, or a related engineering or engineering technology discipline, and At least two (2) years of experience in laboratory operations, research management, or facility coordination, or Equivalent combination of education and directly related experience. Preferred Education, Knowledge, Skills and Experience Advanced Degree : Master’s or PhD in a related science or engineering field. Digital Engineering Expertise : Familiarity with Digital Twin technology, MBSE frameworks, or AI-augmented design workflows. Industry Experience: Demonstrated experience working within a technology hub or managing industry-university collaborative facilities. Strategic Planning : Ability to align facility operations with the broader goals of the North Tryon Tech Hub and regional economic development. Advanced Lab Management: Expertise in managing resources, assets, inventory, budget, preventative maintenance, service contracts, complex workflows, and quality assurance programs. Technical Expertise: Demonstrated knowledge of computer infrastructure, network, and security (e.g., NIST , ISO standards). Necessary Certifications/Licenses N/A Preferred Certifications/Licenses N/A Special Notes to Applicants The finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check and/or a Motor Vehicle Report The Search Committee will not contact references without first verifying permission with the finalist. Please ensure your resume reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers to the supplemental questions. UNC Charlotte Benefits Information: https://hr.charlotte.edu/benefits/benefits-overview/ Posting Open Date 06/12/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Proposed Hire Date 08/03/2026 If time-limited please indicate appointment end date Contact Information Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? UNC Charlotte Website HERC Job Board Inside Higher Education Mitratech Circa (formerly known as Local JobNetwork) Another Website Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Other Where did you learn about this posting? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a bachelor's degree from an appropriately accredited institution, preferably in computer science, systems engineering, information technology, or a related engineering or engineering technology discipline, and \r\nAt least two (2) years of experience in laboratory operations, research management, or facility coordination, or an equivalent combination of education and directly related experience? Yes, at least a bachelor's degree from an appropriately accredited institution, preferably in computer science, systems engineering, information technology, or a related engineering or engineering technology discipline, and at least two (2) years of exper Yes, an associate's degree degree from an appropriately accredited institution, preferably in computer science, systems engineering, information technology, or a related engineering or engineering technology discipline, and  At least four (4) years of exp Yes, a high school diploma/GED and  At least six (6) years of experience in laboratory operations, research management, or facility coordination, No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Contact Information for References Optional Documents 9201 University City Blvd \r\nCharlotte, NC 28223 © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Charlotte. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
