    "https://jobs.charlotte.edu/postings/70306": {
      "title": "Assistant Athletic Director of Compliance",
      "description": "UNC Charlotte Applicant Site | Assistant Athletic Director of Compliance Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Application Process State of NC Salary Chart Campus Security Report Student Employment Assistant Athletic Director of Compliance Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check and/or a Motor Vehicle Report The Search Committee will not contact references without first verifying permission with the finalist. Please ensure your resume reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers to the supplemental questions. UNC Charlotte Benefits Information: https://hr.charlotte.edu/benefits/benefits-overview/ Position Information General Information Position Number 000100 Vacancy Open to All Candidates Working Title Assistant Athletic Director of Compliance Position Designation EHRA Non-Faculty Employment Type Permanent - Full-time Months per Year 12 Work Schedule Monday – Friday, 8:00 am – 5:00 pm, some nights and weekends as necessary. Hours per week 40 FLSA Status Exempt Division Athletics Department Athletics (Adm) Work Location SAC Salary Range Primary Purpose of Department The mission of the Athletic Department at the University of North Carolina at Charlotte is to operate within the perspective of the overall educational programs. With a balanced program that supports equitable opportunities for all students and staff, the department promotes a total person concept that provides its student-athletes with the necessary tools to be successful in academic, athletic, and social settings. The Department of Athletics supports the highest ethical standards of the University, the NCAA , and affiliated conference. Primary Purpose of Position This position is responsible for interpreting NCAA rules and regulations and ensuring that UNC Charlotte remains in compliance with those rules. Summary of Position Responsibilities Serve as the primary Athletics Compliance liaison to the institutional Scholarship/Financial Aid Office and athletics CFO . Oversee administration, monitoring, and reconciliation of student-athlete financial aid, including awards, adjustments, scholarship equivalencies, cost of attendance, and outstanding balances. Coordinate financial aid audits and ensure compliance with NCAA , conference, and institutional requirements. Serve as the primary compliance administrator for the College Athlete Payment System ( CAPS ), overseeing the accuracy, reconciliation, monitoring, and timely reporting of required data. Coordinate with the Athletics Business Office and other campus partners regarding revenue-sharing agreements, payments, roster information, and required CAPS certifications/attestations. Monitor roster and revenue-sharing requirements and maintain appropriate internal controls and documentation. Coordinate NCAA initial and continuing eligibility certification in partnership with the Athletics Academic Center, Registrar, and other campus offices. Guide transfer eligibility and prepare NCAA waivers as assigned. Coordinate collection and submission of NCAA APR , GSR , and other required NCAA , conference, and institutional reports. Serve as the primary compliance contact for assigned sport programs and provide rules interpretations and education to coaches, staff, and student-athletes. Investigate potential NCAA violations, research applicable precedent and penalties, and prepare required NCAA /conference reporting. Monitor and review compliance documentation, including CARA logs, recruiting activities, participation records, and other required forms and reports to ensure adherence to NCAA , conference, and institutional requirements Assist with implementation of NCAA legislation, College Sports Commission requirements, and other regulatory changes; perform additional duties as assigned by the Senior Associate Athletic Director for Governance and Regulatory Affairs. Minimum Education/Experience Bachelor’s degree and one year of compliance work in a Division I College/University. Preferred Education, Knowledge, Skills and Experience Master’s degree preferred. Knowledge of financial aid policy and procedures and NCAA eligibility process, and legislation preferred. Experience with ARMS software. Experience with NCAA applications such as LSDBi & RSRO . Necessary Certifications/Licenses Preferred Certifications/Licenses Special Notes to Applicants The finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check and/or a Motor Vehicle Report The Search Committee will not contact references without first verifying permission with the finalist. Please ensure your resume reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers to the supplemental questions. UNC Charlotte Benefits Information: https://hr.charlotte.edu/benefits/benefits-overview/ Posting Open Date 09/01/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Proposed Hire Date 10/01/2026 If time-limited please indicate appointment end date Contact Information Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? UNC Charlotte Website HERC Job Board Inside Higher Education Mitratech Circa (formerly known as Local JobNetwork) Another Website Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Other Where did you learn about this posting? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a bachelor’s degree and 1 year of compliance work at a Division I College or University? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Contact Information for References Optional Documents 9201 University City Blvd \r\nCharlotte, NC 28223 © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Charlotte. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.charlotte.edu/postings/69626": {
      "title": "Executive Director of Budget and Personnel",
      "description": "UNC Charlotte Applicant Site | Executive Director of Budget and Personnel Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Application Process State of NC Salary Chart Campus Security Report Student Employment Executive Director of Budget and Personnel Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check and/or a Motor Vehicle Report The Search Committee will not contact references without first verifying permission with the finalist. Please ensure your resume reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers to the supplemental questions. Information about the university’s benefits package can be found at https://hr.charlotte/benefits Position Information General Information Position Number 001936 Vacancy Open to All Candidates Working Title Executive Director of Budget and Personnel Position Designation EHRA Non-Faculty Employment Type Permanent - Full-time Months per Year 12 Work Schedule 8:00 am – 5:00 pm, Monday – Friday, with occasional evening and weekend hours as needed. Hours per week 40 FLSA Status Exempt Division Research Department Div of Research (Adm) Work Location Grigg Hall, Room #268 Salary Range $115,000 - $135,000 Primary Purpose of Department The Office of Budget and Personnel is a unit within the Division of Research that supports the Division’s vision and mission as related to research growth. The Office of Budget and Personnel provides management and oversight of all Financial and Human Resource initiatives for all units within the Division of Research. Primary Purpose of Position Budget and Financial Management Human Resources Management Millennial Campus Business Office Management The Executive Director of Budget and Personnel serves as the Division-level budget director, human resources officer/liaison, and Millennial Campus Business Officer for the Division of Research (DR). The Executive Director plans, directs, implements and administers fiscal procedures, methods, and systems of the University to maintain compliance with University policies and procedures for all sources of funds and human resources work; the Executive Director coordinates with Human Resources to manage the Division’s staff and student personnel and salary matters, ensuring adherence to and compliance with required processes for recruitment, selection, work plan creation, and periodic performance review for all positions within DR. Summary of Position Responsibilities The Executive Director of Budget and Personnel works closely with the Vice Chancellor and Associate Vice Chancellor to develop the Division or Research’s annual operating budget; leads the division annual budget call process; reviews and advises senior leadership on budget requests and presents to the Vice Chancellor and Associate Vice Chancellor; works with senior leadership within decentralized business office operation to meet division and university strategic goals; monitors budget spending, communicates to Vice Chancellor and Associate Vice Chancellor on departmental and divisional budget; serves as DR’s internal controller and approver for budget management and business processes; ensures effective controls are in place and followed; develops and analyzes budget reports as required; manages and oversees the funding of internal grant programs; manages a team of direct report staff while accomplishing these duties; develops procedures that meet the business need of the units within the Division of Research; manages and oversees the Millennial Campus Business Office operation. Executive Director serves as the Human Resources Manager and Liaison for the Division of Research staff (~92); HR liaison and support for DR staff; business continuity planning; initiates, reviews, and approves all HR processes for DR; manages, oversees, and troubleshoots as possible, in coordination with the campus HR Office, the annual performance evaluation system process for DR departments; maintains and manages HR files as a decentralized business office; works with HR Office as needed for SHRA and EHRA positions, including reviewing JCAT data, etc.; serves as the department timekeeper in KRONOS system, delegated authority for Personnel actions from Vice Chancellor; manages a team of direct report staff managing HR initiatives; conducts and oversees Division annual performance evaluation process to meet campus HR deadlines. Oversees campus-wide Postdoctoral Fellows Program hiring processes. The Executive Director leads the Millennial Campus Business Office to manage and oversee the processing of all University Business Partner ( UBP ) legal agreements, invoicing and collection of financials; reporting of financials; manages a team of staff to provide customer service support for UBP’s; responsible for accounting/business standards and practices, policy interpretation and implementation, organization of work and verification of all. The Executive Director serves as a member of the Senior Leadership team; supervises Budget and Personnel Team of six (6) staff; serves as a liaison for Division of Research to numerous external and internal partners as needed; provides and/or initiates written and verbal communications to implement and/or explain policies and procedures; attends campus research activities, business partner events, and miscellaneous events for DR; communicates decisions as they impact internal and external customers; manages the licensing rental agreements and invoicing process for Co-Lab entrepreneurial facility in uptown for external partners; and manages special projects as assigned by the Vice Chancellor and/or Associate Vice Chancellor in any area for the Division of Research. Minimum Education/Experience Master’s Degree with a minimum of five years as a business officer or director of finance; Supervisory experience with staff; or Bachelor’s degree with seven years of experience in fiscal and human resource management. Preferred Education, Knowledge, Skills and Experience Experience in fiscal management in a college or university setting. Knowledge of the North Carolina State budget policies and the State Budget Manual. Knowledge of the State Human Resources policies. Knowledge of University policies and procedures. Experience with Banner, Kronos, Salesforce, PeopleAdmin, SciQuest. Advanced reporting skills. Excellent communication skills, both written and verbal. Excellent organizational skills. Ability to collaborate with a wide range of employees at various levels. Necessary Certifications/Licenses Preferred Certifications/Licenses Special Notes to Applicants The finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check and/or a Motor Vehicle Report The Search Committee will not contact references without first verifying permission with the finalist. Please ensure your resume reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers to the supplemental questions. Information about the university’s benefits package can be found at https://hr.charlotte/benefits Posting Open Date 07/27/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Proposed Hire Date 10/01/2026 If time-limited please indicate appointment end date Contact Information Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? UNC Charlotte Website HERC Job Board Inside Higher Education Mitratech Circa (formerly known as Local JobNetwork) Another Website Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Other Where did you learn about this posting? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a master’s degree with a minimum of five years as a business officer or director of finance; Supervisory experience with staff; or a bachelor’s degree with seven years of experience in fiscal and human resource management? Yes, a master’s degree with a minimum of five years as a business officer or director of finance and supervisory experience with staff. Yes, a bachelor’s degree with seven years of experience in fiscal and human resource management. No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Contact Information for References Optional Documents 9201 University City Blvd \r\nCharlotte, NC 28223 © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Charlotte. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
